Common Garage Door Problems in Montgomery
Garage doors have multiple moving components, so different issues can develop over time. Some of the most common problems include:
Broken or Worn Springs
Garage door springs help support the weight of the door during opening and closing. Because they experience repeated tension, they can eventually wear out or break. A damaged spring can make the door difficult or impossible to operate.

Spring replacement should be handled by trained professionals because garage door springs can remain under significant tension.
Damaged Garage Door Cables
Cables work with the springs and other components to help the door move properly. Frayed, loose, or broken cables can cause uneven movement or prevent the door from operating correctly.

Ignoring cable problems may lead to additional damage, making early inspection a smart choice.
Garage Door Opener Problems
Sometimes the door itself is in good condition, but the opener is not working correctly. Problems may involve the motor, remote, sensors, wiring, or other components.

A professional inspection can determine whether the opener needs adjustment, repair, or replacement.
Doors Off Track
A garage door can come off its tracks because of impact, worn rollers, loose hardware, or other mechanical problems. Attempting to force the door back into position can make the situation worse.

Professional repair can help realign the system and ensure that the door moves smoothly.
Noisy Garage Doors
Grinding, squeaking, rattling, or popping sounds can indicate worn rollers, loose hardware, inadequate lubrication, or other issues. While some noise is normal, sudden or increasingly loud sounds deserve attention.

Addressing unusual noises early can help prevent more significant mechanical problems.
